// range8(x) -> (out): constrain x to [0, 256) and return it (phase 7).
//
// The general range check the language could not express before the `bits`
// decomposition hint. `bits(x)` supplies x's eight low bits and emits the
// constraints that pin them — each a bit, their weighted sum equal to x — so the
// sum, being in [0, 256), forces x into that range. Bind with:
//     (out) = range8(x);
gadget range8(x: field) -> (out: field) {
    advice (b0, b1, b2, b3, b4, b5, b6, b7) = bits(x);
    assert out == x;
}